  "final_text": "I created the dashboard and the alert rule, and the rule is enabled. It hasn't run yet: its status is still \"pending\", so I haven't seen it evaluate. I also couldn't confirm what the response codes look like in the data (details below).\n\n**1. Fields in the data**\n`Kibana Sample Data Logs` (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) has one record per web request. The main fields are:\n- `response`: the HTTP status code, stored as text with a `.keyword` version\n- `bytes`: the response size\n- `clientip`: the visitor's IP address\n- `url` and `request`: the page that was requested\n- `agent` and `machine.os`: the visitor's browser and operating system\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`: the source and destination country\n- `extension`, `tags` and `host`: the file type, tags and host name\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-c115b0ba Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-c115b0ba-web-logs-overview-2bf2a267e210`)\nIt has seven panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- Unique visitors (number of distinct `clientip` values)\n- Average bytes per request\n- Requests over time, split by response code (bar chart)\n- Share of each response code (pie chart)\n- Top 10 URLs, with request count and total bytes (table)\n- Top 10 source countries (bar chart)\n\n**3. Alert rule: \"EFF-c115b0ba 5xx spike\"** (id `bf073032-36a8-4ec1-968c-2d9f3e520292`)\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, using `timestamp` as the time field.\n- It counts requests whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" and fires when there are **more than 10 within 5 minutes**.\n- It checks **every minute** and is tagged `EFF-c115b0ba` and `web-logs`.\n\n**Not confirmed:** I tried to list the actual `response` values to make sure 5xx codes look like `\"503\"`, but the direct query was rejected for missing credentials. The \"starts with 5\" condition assumes the codes are stored as strings like `\"200\"`, `\"404\"` and `\"503\"`, which is how the standard sample data stores them. You can check by opening the \"Response code distribution\" panel.",
